{:id :EACL-FORMAL-070
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "snapshot-protocol/caller-runtime-option-injection"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :false-grant
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before snapshot option closure"]
 :affected-backends
 [:shared :datomic :datahike :datascript]
 :root-cause
 "The public snapshot wrapper passed an empty internal options map, but the public protocol method also accepted caller-supplied options and merged them over trusted client runtime dependencies. A caller could replace public-ID resolution while retaining the client's trusted database and schema."
 :fix
 "Keep the protocol arity for implementers but require an exactly empty options map in the shared client before basis selection. Caller requests can choose only the documented consistency descriptor; trusted codecs, clocks, caches, and security configuration remain captured from make-client."
 :closing-evidence
 ["SnapshotOptionBoundary.EmptyPublicSnapshotCapturesTrustedRuntime"
  "SnapshotOptionBoundary.ClosedProtocolRejectsEveryCallerOption"
  "eacl.formal.executed-mutation-controls/snapshot-option-injection-killed?"
  "eacl.datascript.contract-test/public-request-shapes-fail-closed-before-datascript-mutation-test"]}
